+# Windows ARM64 Port
+
+This branch, `arm64-port`, makes libffi 3.8.0 (the MSYS2 recipe tree) build and pass its tests natively on Windows ARM64 (`aarch64`) with MSVC. The work was done natively on a Snapdragon X Elite host.
+
+The sources already supported Windows ARM64 (`src/aarch64/win64_armasm.S` for MSVC, and `sysv.S` with the MSYS2 Cygwin patch). Most of the port fixes ABI bugs in that code and makes the stale MSBuild project build again.
+
+## Summary of Changes
+### Build System
+- `msvc_build/aarch64/Ffi_staticLib.vcxproj`:
+  - toolset is now `$(DefaultPlatformToolset)` (v143 fallback) and the SDK is `10.0`
+  - adds `tramp.c`, `raw_api.c` and `java_raw_api.c`
+  - removes the separate `dlmalloc.c`, which `closures.c` already includes
+  - fixes the `ffi_cfi.h`/`ffi_common.h` paths
+  - the armasm64 step now writes `$(IntDir)win64_armasm.obj`; an escaped `/I"src\"` quote had swallowed `-o`
+  - uses `FFI_STATIC_BUILD` instead of `FFI_BUILDING_DLL`, and Debug no longer defines `NDEBUG`
+- `msvc_build/aarch64/Ffi_staticLib.sln`: removes the x86/x64 solution platforms that were mapped onto ARM64.
+- `msvc_build/aarch64/aarch64_include/{ffi.h,fficonfig.h}`: regenerated from a 3.8.0 configure run. The old ones were from 3.3-rc0, so `FFI_TYPE_VECTOR` and `FFI_TYPE_*INT128` were missing.
+- `include/ffi_common.h`: `FFI_ALIGN_DOWN` masks with `~(a - 1)` instead of `-a`. The old form triggered C4146, which `/sdl` turns into an error.
+- `testsuite/Makefile.am`, `testsuite/Makefile.in`: list the two new tests.
+
+### Source Code
+- ABI fixes:
+  - `src/aarch64/win64_armasm.S`: `extend_hfa_type` loaded the 3rd and 4th vectors of an HVA from offset 16 instead of 32. As a result, MSVC `ffi_call` passed the wrong values for HVA3/HVA4 arguments.
+  - `src/aarch64/ffi.c`, Windows ARM64 variadic calls: these use no FP/SIMD registers and treat HFAs/HVAs as plain composites, which means:
+    - pack up to 16 bytes into X registers
+    - pass larger ones by reference
+    - split them between x7 and the stack when they don't fit
+  - libffi instead gave each HFA member its own X register. A variadic call with an HFA argument crashed (0xC0000005); both `ffi_call` and closures are fixed.
+- Platform guards:
+  - `src/aarch64/ffi.c`: `FlushInstructionCache` is used for every Windows compiler (MSVC, mingw GCC/clang, Cygwin). libgcc's `__clear_cache` reads `CTR_EL0`, which traps in user mode.
+  - `src/dlmalloc.c`: does not redeclare `_InterlockedCompareExchange`/`_InterlockedExchange` on `_M_ARM64`, because they are intrinsics there.
+- Tests:
+  - `testsuite/libffi.call/ffitest.h`: `PRIuPTR` is `"llu"` on 64-bit MSVC.
+  - New `testsuite/libffi.call/va_hfa.c`: variadic float/double HFAs of every size after 0-7 integer args, for both `ffi_call` and closures. It is an expected failure on aarch64 Cygwin; see Limitations.
+  - New `testsuite/libffi.call/hva_neon.c`: HVAs of 2-4 `float32x4_t` for both `ffi_call` and closures. This is the regression test for the armasm fix.
+
+### CI/CD
+None. The tree has no CI configuration.
+
+### New Files
+- `testsuite/libffi.call/va_hfa.c`
+- `testsuite/libffi.call/hva_neon.c`
+- `benchmarks/base_bench_win_arm.json`, `benchmarks/base_bench_win_arm.meta.json`
+
+## Build Steps (ARM64)
+Prerequisites:
+- Visual Studio 2022 or later with the MSVC ARM64 build tools and the Windows 11 SDK (tested with VS 18, MSVC 14.51, v145)
+- MSYS2 with `make` and autotools, for the autotools route
+
+### Build
+Autotools + msvcc.sh produces `libffi-8.dll` and `libffi-8.lib`. Run it from an MSYS2 bash started inside `vcvarsarm64.bat`, with `MSYS2_PATH_TYPE=inherit`:
+```sh
+mkdir build-arm64 && cd build-arm64
+/path/to/libffi/configure --host=aarch64-w64-mingw32 \
+  CC="/path/to/libffi/msvcc.sh -marm64" CXX="/path/to/libffi/msvcc.sh -marm64" \
+  CCAS="/path/to/libffi/msvcc.sh -marm64" LD=link CPPFLAGS="-DFFI_BUILDING_DLL" \
+  CPP="cl -nologo -EP" CXXCPP="cl -nologo -EP" --enable-shared --enable-static
+make -j4
+```
+MSBuild produces the static `Ffi_staticLib_arm64.lib`. Consumers must define `FFI_STATIC_BUILD`.
+```powershell
+& "C:\Program Files\Microsoft Visual Studio\18\Community\MSBuild\Current\Bin\arm64\MSBuild.exe" msvc_build\aarch64\Ffi_staticLib.sln /t:Rebuild /p:Configuration=Release /p:Platform=ARM64
+```
+Build output:
+- `build-arm64/.libs/libffi-8.dll` and `libffi-8.lib`
+- `msvc_build/aarch64/ARM64/<Config>/Ffi_staticLib_arm64.lib`, or the `/p:OutDir` you pass
+
+### Run Tests
+DejaGnu is not available for MSVC on this host, so the testsuite was driven by a Python runner. For each test it:
+- follows `dg-do run`/`dg-output`/`dg-options`/`dg-skip-if`
+- compiles with `cl -nologo -W3 -MD` and the per-suite flags from the `.exp` files
+- runs the test and checks the exit code and the `dg-output` regex
+
+With DejaGnu available, the equivalent is:
+```sh
+make check RUNTESTFLAGS="call.exp closure.exp bhaible.exp"
+```
+Expected: 345 passed, 0 failed, 42 unsupported.
+
+### Run Benchmarks
+The microbenchmark is a small `ffi_call`/closure loop. Build it with `cl -O2 -MD`; it is not part of the tree. Results are in `benchmarks/base_bench_win_arm.json`, and the commands are recorded in `base_bench_win_arm.meta.json`.
+
